WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.350
For Turkey, there's dark clouds on the horizon.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:12.610
In the aftermath of the failed coup, President
Recep Tayyip Erdogan has launched a crackdown

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:17.900
that would make even Vladimir Putin in Russia
blush, rounding up tens of thousands of people.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:23.980
Not only the alleged perpetrators, but he's
sacked constitutional court judges, dismissed

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.000
1,500 university deans, gone after journalists,
and so forth.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.000
In the fight against the Islamic State, this
is going to have reverberations.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.669
Recep Tayyip Erdogan wants the United States
to extradite Fethullah Gulen, an Islamic cleric

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:38.480
based in Pennsylvania who he sees as a rival,
and it seems that Erogan is willing to hold

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.760
the U.S. fight against the Islamic State hostage
by, perhaps in the future, denying the U.S.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.960
ability to use the Incirlik air base.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.489
This puts Europe and the United States in
a conundrum.

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:53.039
Because as Turkey's crackdown accelerates,
as Turkey talks about reimposing the death

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:59.010
penalty, the European Union says, "Hey, this
changes the whole EU accession debate.”

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.429
And with regard to the United States, on one
hand, we condemn the coup.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:08.270
But we didn't mean to give an open door for
a crackdown that would purge tens of thousands.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:11.260
So what do you think Erdogan is going to do
next?

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:15.480
Let us know in the comments, and let us know
any other topics you'd like AEI scholars to

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.960
address in 60 seconds.

